Connect a monitoring signal to a proportionate response (@cm-monitoring-response: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN", #source "../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/GUM-Conformity.lingua#r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY", #clean-manufacturing "Maintain-the-claim-through-change-and-restoration.lingua#r_7729DVQH9XYHQKGEE5QHCK8NJB") { r_14SFA69Q0ZBZ89SWK9K08X0QR0
**Read:** [Measurement Process Characterization — NIST/SEMATECH](../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/Statistical-Handbook.lingua#r_6S3221KSX1KKGPJNXKC3N022NN), section 6.1.4 and measurement-control case studies; [Measurement uncertainty in conformity assessment — JCGM 106](../../../inquiry/metrology/sources/GUM-Conformity.lingua#r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY), the decision being made.

A monitoring system includes what happens after a signal. Identify the affected operation or product interval, preserve the observations and examine the measurement's validity. Distinguish a warning about unusual behavior from evidence that a product requirement has been exceeded.

Response depends on consequence and available evidence. A reference check may reveal an instrument problem; a functional observation may reveal product impact. Returning a chart to its old mean does not by itself establish that previously affected items are acceptable or that the cause has been resolved.

Frequent adjustments in response to ordinary random variation can increase instability. Conversely, dismissing every signal as noise can hide a persistent change. Evaluate the response rule with the detector, including delays, workload and consequences of false and missed signals.

**Work:** Follow a benign simulated excursion from detection through investigation and a justified disposition of the affected evidence and items. Compare an instrument fault with a real process shift. Specify what observation would support return to the intended operation, without pretending that the simulated exercise authorizes work on an actual facility.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
